WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.571
NARRATOR: But imagine seeing
the park with fresh eyes,

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:07.841
and every view a rare
glimpse into a hidden

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:11.378
world just like this one.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:24.791
A black bear and her cubs,
a typical litter of three.

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:31.865
For five months,
she hasn't stirred.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:39.806
Even as their mother slumbered,
the cubs nursed on a rich diet

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.241
of super-fatty milk.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:48.848
Over the winter, her own
weight dropped up to 1/3.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:56.122
How she survived
still stumps us.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:59.926
During hibernation, her heart
rate fell to just eight bits

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:03.530
per minute, and somehow, she
turned much of her bodily waste

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.330
into protein.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.537
In the coming months,
she must fatten

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.372
up on what the forest provides.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:20.580
The survival of the fragile
cubs depends on their mother.

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:23.116
Her survival depends
on the Smokies.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.426
After weeks confined
to a cubbyhole,

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.929
new life makes its
debut in the park.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:43.736
Black bears are born
climbers with strong claws.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:47.540
Even a bear cub negotiates the
trunk like a power lineman.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.748
Their debut draws attention.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.492
Our mom must stay alert.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.264
Coyotes will prey on the cubs.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:15.401
So will bobcats.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:27.780
At night, the treetops
offer refuge from predators

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:28.581
that can't climb.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:36.523
In daylight on the ground,
the cubs are vulnerable,

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.358
so mom won't let them wander.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:45.899
For the next 18 months,
they'll shadow their mother,

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:50.203
their instructor and protector
within a park that safeguards

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.872
them from another enemy, man.

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:02.115
Male cubs will grow
up to be loners

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:03.616
like their long-gone father.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:10.523
Females will rear
their own offspring.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.359
For now, three
wide-eyed toddlers

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:16.429
enter a world made
for them, if they

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.798
learn to make the most of it.

